# PHPStan as CI runs it. One difference from `phpstan.neon`, and it is the only one.
#
# Hyvä is commercial — served from a licensed private Packagist that a public repository has no
# credentials for, and putting them in a public workflow is not a trade worth making. Exactly one
# class stands in the way: `hyva-product-slider` takes `Hyva\Theme\ViewModel\ProductListItem` in
# its constructor. Every other `Hyva\` reference in the repo is in a `.phtml` or an XML file, and
# PHPStan reads neither. `scanFiles` supplies that one signature instead.
#
# Everything else — level, paths, suppressions, the magic-accessor extension — comes from
# `phpstan.neon` unchanged, `scanDirectories: ../generated/code` included. CI compiles that
# directory with `setup:di:compile` before running this, and it is not optional: without it the
# analysis reports 348 `class.notFound`, almost all of them on the `*Factory` classes Magento
# generates rather than ships. An earlier version of this file cleared `scanDirectories` on the
# theory that the suppressions already covered what it held. They do not, and the local run that
# appeared to show otherwise was misleading — on the stand those classes resolve through the
# installation's autoloader whether or not PHPStan is told to scan for them.
#
# Run `phpstan.neon` locally, not this file. On the stand Hyvä is really installed, and checking
# `hyva-product-slider` against the real signature instead of our copy of it is the point of
# keeping both. `tools/phpstan/test/stub-drift.php` is what compares the two.
includes:
    - phpstan.neon

parameters:
    scanFiles:
        - tools/phpstan/stubs/Hyva/Theme/ViewModel/ProductListItem.php
